==English==

===Etymology===
Since the maximum number of balls before a {{l|en|walk|id=baseball}} is three, and the maximum number of strikes before a [[strikeout]] is two, neither number can increase without ending the at-bat.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|baseball}} An {{l|en|at-bat}} with a count of three {{l|en|ball|balls|id=baseball}} and two {{l|en|strike|strikes|id=baseball}}.
#: {{ux|en|'''Full count''', two outs, bottom of the ninth, the bags are jammed, 2-2 tie…}}

====Usage notes====
* Occasionally used in the form ''the count is full''.